From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:47:46 -0500
Subject: fix: a second window's corner buttons show on Windows; links from
 other apps can open as a peek (S-416, S-417)

The window's buttons at the corner (sidebar Y54; GitHub issue 45, a comment
on 0.4.0 beta 8): the corner's event monitor reports the pointer in screen
coordinates, which the corner read as the window's. A maximized window sits
at the screen's top-left and its buttons showed; a window at an offset -- a
moved tab's, New Blank Window, any cascaded one -- missed its corner by that
offset, and its buttons never showed while the frame's own were hidden. The
pointer is now converted from the screen.

Links from other apps as a peek (little E11, settings T54; GitHub issue 74):
"Open links from other apps as a peek", off by default, opens such a link
as a peek over the active tab of the window it would have opened over, over
the page or in a small window as "Show a peek" says, and brings that window
to the front. With no normal window, or a peek that cannot show, the little
window opens as before. The peek over the page now registers with the first
navigation, so a peek no pin started finds it.

Why: GitHub issue 45 (a second window could only be closed by dragging its
tab back) and issue 74 (the reporter asked; the owner agreed to an option,
off by default), 2026-11-04.
Removable when: never as behaviour.
